<title>AUSTRALIA: BankWest sets A$100 mln bond-SBC Warburg.</title>
<headline>BankWest sets A$100 mln bond-SBC Warburg.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>SBC Warburg said it has lead managed a A$100 million domestic bond for BankWest.</p>
<p>The issue, which matures on November 15, 2001, pays a 7.75 percent coupon and was priced on a reoffer basis at 35 basis points over the Australian Treasury's November 2001 bond.</p>
<p>The bonds were issued off BankWest's domestic MTN programme.</p>
<p>--Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
